<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vansda National Park</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1979</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vansda National Park is a protected forest in Navsari district of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the Ambika river near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ghats">Western Ghats</a>. Declared a national park in 1979, it covers about 24 square kilometres of former forest of the princely state of Bansda, with moist deciduous woodland of teak and bamboo that shelters leopards and many birds.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vansda-national-park.jpg" alt="Vansda National Park" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was સતિષચંદ્ર at Gujarati Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vansda_N_Park6.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
